>In article <82660@bu.edu> Lnd@cs.bu.edu writes:
>>Say, things should be different between midnight and dawn ...

It's a little known fact, but things are different.  (Well, not exactly 
between midnight and dawn, but...)

If you are playing nethack any time during the midnight hour (i.e. 12:00 AM
to 12:59 AM), and get attacked by anything undead, you might notice that it
does more damage than usual.  This is because during the midnight hour, if 
an undead creature hits you it will do double damage!  If it would normally
do, say, 2d4 damage (or 2-8 points of damage), it will instead do 4d4 damage
(or 4-16 points of damage) during the midnight hour.  So... watch out for 
those undead creatures if you're burning the late night nethack oil!

